{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:0359:title", "parent_tag": "0359", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "risk_level": "R1", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Nagata schemes, reprise", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-nagata}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:7911c2fffabb4a951033097c95ff6b396e63f09b885df1ff8c7d9b49da03250b", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5621de9e0ae79c5c31c16b692dbe60a7d0dd82798251472f135582fce7a9ab98", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:0359:prose-0001", "parent_tag": "0359", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSee Properties, Section <REF_0001> for the definitions\nand basic properties of Nagata and universally Japanese schemes.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "REF_0001": "\\ref{properties-section-nagata}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:c9d4356c65231bba1c48d80f46b5ee459502f986bacc0d949b0fd5506d456351", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:48392ea916575047ee1b300638306092532eab5ce8bde34295a0953b67cf607f", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:035A:statement", "parent_tag": "0359", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism.\nIf <MATH_0002> is Nagata and <MATH_0003> locally of finite type then <MATH_0004> is Nagata.\nIf <MATH_0005> is universally Japanese\nand <MATH_0006> locally of finite type then <MATH_0007> is universally Japanese.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-type-nagata}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:7423896b8ef5db97cb7a6c4d9f837b049f0c62494fccca87fe1fb51497ab21f7", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5932b7135c319a1a5aa07795bdcd0a4b2c58185e34d7d6bd897752ebbe3d7672", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3e5204c1c961551b794fedcfdfbb6b05641e5f59362429987fa341c0863d42ed"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:035A:proof", "parent_tag": "0359", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "For ``universally Japanese'' this follows from\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nFor ``Nagata'' this follows from\nAlgebra, Proposition <REF_0002>.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-universally-japanese}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-proposition-nagata-universally-japanese}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:84d98b0b23113b9ee66e721c6a0f0547b8a364be137511fa53ea6b6f65f9bcab", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dd65b158a9d5d3c73b92d66793e018fc686f2d94c36bd45579147f59f9bed484", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:035B:statement", "parent_tag": "0359", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "The following types of schemes are Nagata.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Any scheme locally of finite type over a field.\n<STRUCT_0003> Any scheme locally of finite type over a Noetherian complete local ring.\n<STRUCT_0004> Any scheme locally of finite type over <MATH_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0005> Any scheme locally of finite type over a Dedekind ring of\ncharacteristic zero.\n<STRUCT_0006> And so on.\n<STRUCT_0007>\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathbf{Z}$", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-ubiquity-nagata}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:f35a94c0657c8bb481f86edbc31752dc437e76a1f17737876b3d0dd17db1cad0", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4c89c2648adb3276c5c529c0462d3795e4a41b9e6e6aef1f69bc4b099346985f", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ce27841503e12e6f65ff4227a2873a91c0b2ca140a4ec8c562a0bff31b2b3d9b"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:035B:proof", "parent_tag": "0359", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "By Lemma <REF_0001> we only need to show that\nthe rings mentioned above are Nagata rings. For this see\nAlgebra, Proposition <REF_0002>.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-finite-type-nagata}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-proposition-ubiquity-nagata}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:9dda6a0c168fd0c0a8826ca74192981a35bfbf2280635fc547635d3bb2b446a2", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:84f9e8008d5a8907c95b30f6be9ec586a9582a1651ca261a7b1bfd6d5b75ba92", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
